  "answer_core": "Run a pre-buy test this week with the three customers who signaled interest: name a specific price, require a three-month prepay, and write down the pass/fail bar before you reach out (e.g., two of three commit within 14 days). In that same 14-day window, quickly check two additional things: who already competes in this workflow space and what it would cost to freeze, sunset, or migrate your 22 current customers. Those are go/no-go inputs alongside the pre-buy test.\n\nHave the hard conversations now because they unlock the decision. Tell your CS employee you are seriously exploring a pivot, that the next two weeks are uncertain, and that if you proceed you will likely need to part ways with a severance package. Notify your former co-founder as a courtesy—share the plan, but make clear you are informing her, not requesting approval; 15% passive equity does not confer a veto on strategy.\n\nIf the pre-buy bar clears and the competitive/migration checks do not reveal fatal flaws, commit: pivot to the workflow tool with a concrete transition plan for the existing 22 customers (freeze development, set sunset or migration terms, communicate timelines). If the test fails, do not pivot. Use the remaining runway to find a different path forward rather than gambling on unvalidated demand.",
